From 95e4a43055c2acf22902ea0eb56925ebf19e6740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:28:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] volumes: preserve CSI mount properties through guest mounting

Carry readonly, filesystem options and fsGroup from mountInfo.json through
the existing proxy volume scan to guest mounts. Decode only the fields in
use; legacy records without readonly keep their writable default and
unknown metadata extensions remain compatible.

Apply readonly to the filesystem and container bind, skip fsGroup changes
on readonly volumes and refuse to format them. Reuse the existing fsGroup
helper and volume test fixtures without introducing a versioned contract,
attachment cache or confidential workspace policy.

Signed-off-by: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>

Co-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
